.TH SCOVILLE 1 "2026-09" "scoville" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scoville \- rate how dangerous a shell command is, before you run it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scoville
.RI [ command ...]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scores commands by how much damage they could do, on a named scale, with
the reasoning shown: which rule fired, and which amplifiers (a wildcard, a
production context, sudo) multiplied it.
.PP
Commands come from the arguments, from a script with
.BR \-\-file ,
or from standard input with
.BR \- .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-f " FILE" ", " \-\-file " FILE"
Analyse a script file.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
.B text
for humans,
.B json
for anything downstream (default text).
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " SCALE"
How to name the levels:
.B bands
(safe to critical) or
.B peppers
(bell pepper to carolina reaper). Text output only.
.TP
.BI \-\-fail\-on " LEVEL"
Exit 1 when any command reaches this level.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Treat unrecognised commands as medium risk.
.TP
.B \-\-introspect
Resolve hidden image and container entrypoints via a read-only
.BR "docker inspect" ,
and ask the current Kubernetes context what it is allowed to do.
.TP
.BI \-\-kube\-timeout " SEC"
Bound on one
.B "kubectl auth can-i"
call under
.BR \-\-introspect .
A timeout scores as if it had not been asked.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
One line per command.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show zero-weight factors too.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Never colourise. A non-tty and
.I NO_COLOR
already disable it.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Override file. The default is the nearest
.I .scovillerc
at or above the analysed file's directory.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Ignore any
.I .scovillerc
that would otherwise be discovered.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-rules
Print every rule and amplifier, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-why " RULE"
Print the long form for one rule or amplifier id, then exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .scovillerc
Per-project overrides, discovered upwards from the analysed file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Scored; no command reached
.BR \-\-fail\-on .
.TP
.B 1
A command reached
.BR \-\-fail\-on .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Score one command:
.PP
.RS
.B scoville 'rm -rf /var/lib/data'
.RE
.PP
Gate a runbook:
.PP
.RS
.B scoville \-f deploy.sh \-\-fail\-on high
.RE
.PP
Explain a rule:
.PP
.RS
.B scoville \-\-why SC-014
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shellcheck (1).
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/scoville
.UE
